Fixed. `src/tax.js` now normalizes the country code before the rate lookup:

```js
export function taxFor(cents, country) {
  const code = String(country).toUpperCase();
  return Math.round(cents * RATES[code].rate);
}
```

- **Cause:** invoice 88121 arrived with `country=at`; the rates map only had uppercase keys, so `RATES["at"]` was `undefined` and `.rate` threw.
- **Fix:** normalize the code in `taxFor`, so any casing resolves.
- **Regression test:** added `country codes are matched case-insensitively` in `tests/tax.test.js`; all 7 tests pass.

